From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:03:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Reapply "ata: ahci: force 32-bit DMA for JMicron
 JMB582/JMB585"

This reverts commit 803e1c8ebae9, the backport of upstream commit
6b28e0e7a073 ("Revert "ata: ahci: force 32-bit DMA for JMicron
JMB582/JMB585""), which came with the Proxmox-7.0-20261116 base in
7.0.14-30.

Since then, the host's ahci driver uses 64-bit DMA for these
controllers and writes the upper halves of the command list and FIS
receive addresses into PxCLBU and PxFBU. A JMB585 passed through to a
VM stopped working with 7.0.14-30: the guest binds its ahci driver, but
every port fails with "softreset failed (1st FIS failed)" or "SATA link
down", and the host logs no IOMMU fault. The quirk removal is the only
functional AHCI change between 7.0.14-29 and 7.0.14-30. The likely
mechanism is that the upper halves survive the vfio-pci reset, and a
guest kernel that forces 32-bit DMA for the JMB585 but does not clear
the upper halves yet, which upstream 82e47533221d added (for example
Linux 6.12.83 to 6.12.111), only writes the lower halves. The
controller then fetches commands and posts FISes at wrong guest
addresses.

With the quirk, the host uses 32-bit DMA and writes zero to the upper
halves, as 82e47533221d is in our base, like all 7.0 kernels up to
7.0.14-29 did. Upstream dropped the quirk because the 64-bit DMA
corruption it worked around comes from enhanced atomics on AMD NBIO
7.7 and 7.11 root ports, which 4fde44822512 ("x86/PCI: Disable enhanced
atomics on AMD NBIO 7.7 and 7.11"), also in our base, now disables.
Keeping the quirk thus only costs 64-bit DMA for these controllers on
the host.

Link: https://bugzilla.proxmox.com/show_bug.cgi?id=8367
Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
---
 drivers/ata/ahci.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ata/ahci.c b/drivers/ata/ahci.c
index bffe50a109b88f72c420218648b6afb184b49bcc..9b8c0935001cb35e9b6603dc6d4e4b683de1a905 100644
--- a/drivers/ata/ahci.c
+++ b/drivers/ata/ahci.c
@@ -68,6 +68,7 @@ enum board_ids {
 	/* board IDs for specific chipsets in alphabetical order */
 	board_ahci_al,
 	board_ahci_avn,
+	board_ahci_jmb585,
 	board_ahci_mcp65,
 	board_ahci_mcp77,
 	board_ahci_mcp89,
@@ -212,6 +213,15 @@ static const struct ata_port_info ahci_port_info[] = {
 		.udma_mask	= ATA_UDMA6,
 		.port_ops	= &ahci_avn_ops,
 	},
+	/* JMicron JMB582/585: 64-bit DMA is broken, force 32-bit */
+	[board_ahci_jmb585] = {
+		AHCI_HFLAGS	(AHCI_HFLAG_IGN_IRQ_IF_ERR |
+				 AHCI_HFLAG_32BIT_ONLY),
+		.flags		= AHCI_FLAG_COMMON,
+		.pio_mask	= ATA_PIO4,
+		.udma_mask	= ATA_UDMA6,
+		.port_ops	= &ahci_ops,
+	},
 	[board_ahci_mcp65] = {
 		AHCI_HFLAGS	(AHCI_HFLAG_NO_FPDMA_AA | AHCI_HFLAG_NO_PMP |
 				 AHCI_HFLAG_YES_NCQ),
@@ -944,6 +954,14 @@ static const struct pci_device_id ahci_pci_tbl[] = {
 		/* Elkhart Lake AHCI */
 		PCI_VDEVICE(INTEL, 0x4b63),
 		.driver_data = board_ahci_pcs_quirk,
+	}, {
+		/* JMicron JMB582/585: force 32-bit DMA (broken 64-bit implementation) */
+		PCI_VDEVICE(JMICRON, 0x0582),
+		.driver_data = board_ahci_jmb585,
+
+	}, {
+		PCI_VDEVICE(JMICRON, 0x0585),
+		.driver_data = board_ahci_jmb585,
 	}, {
 		/* JMicron 360/1/3/5/6, match class to avoid IDE function */
 		PCI_DEVICE(PCI_VENDOR_ID_JMICRON, PCI_ANY_ID),
